    p=ROOT/'START HERE.txt';text=p.read_text();a=text.index('LOCAL INFERENCE RESULT\n');b=text.index('TRY ADVERTISING ASSISTANT\n',a);p.write_text(text[:a]+'LOCAL INFERENCE RESULT\nTwo local API replies correctly explain the actual two-client shared-resource wait/load/wake path and its controlled-fixture limits. One evidence call each, about17s each. Main-scene synchronization/fullgame/nativeChat remain unproved. Default model/prompt unchanged and model idle.\n\nTry: Can both resource callers really wait for and share the same load now, or are the ready flags still faked?\n\nExact exchanges and review:\n'+str(audit/'prompts-and-responses.txt')+'\n\n'+text[b:])
